From: oplus-sukisu_kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] KernelSU: add KSU_SUSFS_PRIORITY_UID_FILTER Kconfig

Companion to sukisu-builtin-priority-filter-stub.patch: the builtin tree
references the priority uid filter, but the SUSFS version we build against
does not define its Kconfig symbol. Declare it here, default n, so the
feature stays off unless explicitly enabled.

Local compatibility shim, not an upstream patch.

diff --git a/kernel/Kconfig b/kernel/Kconfig
index db57137..bb67381 100644
--- a/kernel/Kconfig
+++ b/kernel/Kconfig
@@ -113,6 +113,11 @@ config KSU_SUSFS_OPEN_REDIRECT
 	  - OPEN_REDIRECT does not bypass some detections by default, but users can work with SUS_KSTAT to bypass them.
 	  - Effective only on processes with pre-defined uid scheme.
 
+config KSU_SUSFS_PRIORITY_UID_FILTER
+	bool "Enable priority uid filter (getpriority uid hiding)"
+	depends on KSU_SUSFS
+	default n
+
 config KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP
 	bool "Enable to hide some mmapped real file from different proc maps interfaces"
 	depends on KSU_SUSFS
